<p>I really, really want to +1 this. I love the idea, especially considering just how often we see SCPs generating matter from nowhere willy-nilly. I really like seeing one that actually contemplates what that kind of matter generation would require under currently-understood physical law.</p>
<p>However, I have to agree with A Random Day and MrWrong. The log is just far too convenient, a nice sheaf of exposition just lying around. Furthermore, it's quite a bit too goofy for my tastes, especially all that business about &quot;halved hafnium.&quot; It seems like it takes a guy who has only a very slim understanding of basic science at all, and then just drowns his log in science words. That said, I actually do really like the idea of him misusing E=mc^2 and massively underestimating the energy required.</p>
<p>No vote for now, but if you changed the circumstances and tone of those logs a bit, I feel that I'd be more inclined to upvote.</p>

